---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
    title="Devices"
    description="GPX and FIT courses for a Garmin and other head units."
>
    <main class="shell page">
        <p class="kicker">Devices</p>
        <h1>The computer already knows the map.</h1>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>
                Export a GPX file for almost any head unit, and a FIT course for
                Garmin. In Garmin Connect, import the file under Training, then
                Courses, and sync. Over USB, copy the FIT into
                <code>Garmin/NewFiles</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                Wahoo, Hammerhead, Bryton, and COROS take the same GPX. The course
                name on a Garmin is read from the first 15 characters, so Traceway
                keeps a short device name beside the full one.
            </p>
            <p>
                Automatic publish into a Garmin account waits on their Courses API.
                The file works before that approval.
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>
</Base>
